<article class="env-remark" id="0FWA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FWA">Remark <span data-tag="0FWA">50.21.2</span>.</a> The analogues of Weil Cohomology Theories, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0FI7" data-tag="0FI7">45.12.2</a> (splitting principle) and <a href="/tag/0FI8" data-tag="0FI8">45.12.3</a> (chern classes of tensor products) hold for de Rham Chern classes on quasi-compact and quasi-separated schemes. This is clear as we've shown in the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0FW9" data-tag="0FW9">50.21.1</a> that all the axioms of Weil Cohomology Theories, Section <a href="/tag/0FI4" data-tag="0FI4">45.12</a> are satisfied. </p>
</article>